    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\frac{1}{10}$\n\nRationalise the numerator and cancel the common factor $x^2$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\lim_{x\\to0}\\frac{\\sqrt{x^2+25}-5}{x^2}&=\\lim_{x\\to0}\\frac{(\\sqrt{x^2+25}-5)(\\sqrt{x^2+25}+5)}{x^2(\\sqrt{x^2+25}+5)}\\\\\\lim_{x\\to0}\\frac{\\sqrt{x^2+25}-5}{x^2}&=\\lim_{x\\to0}\\frac{x^2+25-25}{x^2(\\sqrt{x^2+25}+5)}\\\\\\lim_{x\\to0}\\frac{\\sqrt{x^2+25}-5}{x^2}&=\\lim_{x\\to0}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x^2+25}+5}\\\\\\lim_{x\\to0}\\frac{\\sqrt{x^2+25}-5}{x^2}&=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{0^2+25}+5}\\\\\\lim_{x\\to0}\\frac{\\sqrt{x^2+25}-5}{x^2}&=\\frac{1}{10}\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
